WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.360
- The reason I win,

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.690
often,

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:07.590
is because I'm not worried
about the person in the middle.

00:00:08.792 --> 00:00:09.640
Got it?

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:10.473
- [Man] Yeah.

00:00:10.473 --> 00:00:12.210
- I didn't change for them.

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:13.930
They changed for me.

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:15.090
Why?

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:16.871
Because I focused on you.

00:00:16.871 --> 00:00:17.787
(bass music)

00:00:17.787 --> 00:00:19.342
- Yeah.

00:00:19.342 --> 00:00:20.692
- You got your perspective.

00:00:23.812 --> 00:00:24.790
I just wanna be happy.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.040
Don't you wanna be happy?

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:31.310
I'm super excited to be here.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:33.850
Obviously, it's funny,

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:37.300
this is so literal to my world

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:41.910
and it's fun because
yesterday I was in Boston

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:44.240
and I spoke to 600

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:47.170
jewelry store owners

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:50.200
and it felt really warm to
me because they're merchants.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.220
They own a single store
and they sell stuff.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:54.070
And

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:57.560
that, obviously, is very
much where I come from.

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:01.060
And then I get to get
behind it to have this event

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.350
where so many of the people in this room,

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:06.240
the far majority, are doing
what I'm currently doing.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.780
And yesterday was a
lot of fun to reminisce

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:12.100
and challenge myself to
think about what did I do

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.210
when I had no money?

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:15.570
Which is really basically
the framework of the talk,

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:18.140
which is a lotta people in this room

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:19.020
that are familiar with my work,

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:21.230
I talk about a lotta progressive
things, a lot of things.

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:22.760
But the reality is

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:25.880
I always remember when I kept
trying to change the narrative

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:29.990
in 2014, '15, '16, which is
I didn't build Wine Library

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:31.440
through just social media.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:32.870
I did direct mail.

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:34.030
It was search.

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:35.670
It was email marketing.

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:38.150
And I took it way back because
I knew that a lotta people

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:40.430
in the room had no marketing budget.

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:42.990
And it made me remember something
that is super fun for me,

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:46.280
which is literally week
one, out of college,

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:47.880
no marketing budget,

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:52.880
I printed a bunch of 20% off
by the case of wine things

00:01:53.331 --> 00:01:57.120
on a picture I made in
some sort of version

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.380
of old school, not even Photoshop yet.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:02.450
I was so computer illiterate.

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:04.320
I couldn't even know what I was doing.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.840
I remember it had a crab,

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:08.410
literally a crab.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:10.630
There was a default picture of a crab

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:11.760
in a beach.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.540
And I was like, "That's fine."

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:14.850
And I put that there
(laughing)

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:17.970
and then made dotted
lines and it said 20% off

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:20.430
on a case of wine, non sale items.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:24.420
I printed 100 of them, came
to the store the next day,

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:27.670
parked my car, ran in, opened the store,

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:30.290
told one of the kids to
keep an eye on the shop,

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:33.030
and drove to the short hills mall,

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:37.600
and literally put those
flyers on windshields

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:39.033
for an hour and a half.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.620
What's fun about that for me here now is

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:48.440
day one Vayner was super funny.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:49.730
And

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:53.570
the reality is I knew nothing
about the advertising industry

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:56.790
and I had to learn it.

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:57.820
And I had to build.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:01.600
And so it's fun for me to
be challenged to remember

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.250
what I did,

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:05.860
knowing there's a wide
range of people here

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:08.040
who are a one-woman shop,
to people that are trying

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.690
to go from seven to eight figures.

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:12.560
Very honestly, I wanna really move this

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:15.150
into a very aggressive Q&amp;A session

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:16.980
because I think just based

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:18.870
on how many people hit
me up on LinkedIn and

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:21.253
on Twitter over the last
24 hours about this,

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:24.240
the far majority of this
room at least has some level

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:26.650
of context of what I'm gonna
talk about or what I believe.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:28.850
And I don't think that
brings you the most value.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:30.410
I think what brings you the most value

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:33.860
is probably ironically, and
it's fun to see Maribel here

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:37.450
who I've worked very closely
with for quite a long time,

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:41.190
I'm extremely proud of
my operational capability

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:43.590
for all those incredible
things that I heard

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.690
in the intro just now,
which are super fancy

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:49.360
and really surreal for me to think about.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:50.760
What I promise every one of you,

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:52.840
when I think about business,
that I'm most proud of

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:57.118
is 21 years ago, I walked
into my dad's store

00:03:57.118 --> 00:03:58.810
and he decided,

00:03:58.810 --> 00:03:59.910
'cause he was passionate about it,

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:01.920
to renovate the house.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:05.320
This is like family business
shit and I was in charge.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:07.590
Now, I'd been in the
business since I was 14.

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:10.160
Every weekend, every summer
vacation, my dad knew

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:11.900
that I wasn't a schlemiel
and that I was capable.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:14.290
And even the last two years of college,

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:16.330
I was coming home almost every weekend,

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:17.710
putting in work.

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:19.480
But I walked in

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:23.120
and from that day to this second,

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:25.350
I have not raised capital.

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:27.890
I have had a payroll to make.

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:31.130
What blows my mind, this
is not true with Vayner,

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:32.060
because of the scale,

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:36.400
but I didn't even have a
credit line for Wine Library

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.970
and our invoices were due on 30 days

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:41.380
or the distributor would put you on COD,

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.720
cash on delivery, which would
stop you from being able

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:45.640
to buy from any of the distributors.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:49.010
The discipline that I was raised in

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:51.043
to

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:53.833
pay with what you had.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:55.523
Right?

00:04:55.523 --> 00:04:57.090
And so I've scrapped.

00:04:57.090 --> 00:04:58.860
I'm most proud

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.750
that for 21 straight years,
I've had to make payroll

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:03.180
and I have.

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:04.610
Operations.

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:06.000
Building an actual business.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.220
So a lot of fancy other things
have come along the way,

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:11.760
but the connection point
I feel for this room

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:12.910
is quite high.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:16.470
I have a lotta thoughts
about offense and defense,

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:18.773
which is playing out in all of your minds.

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:22.190
And so I'd like to bring
as much value as possible.

00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:24.500
So there's two mics that are lined up,

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:26.493
so I think it's a good idea to line up.

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:29.793
Good.

00:05:31.382 --> 00:05:34.590
And I think just to create
a little more framework

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:36.560
for the Q&amp;A, I know you wanna come out

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:37.620
and frame the Q&amp;A.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:38.453
I just love having you here.

00:05:38.453 --> 00:05:39.660
That was such a good intro.

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:40.560
- [Man] Oh, really?

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:41.513
Thank you.
- Yeah, it's really good.

00:05:41.513 --> 00:05:42.810
(laughing)

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:43.643
- [Man] Can I say one thing?

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:45.288
- Yeah, say three things.
- So you said this,

00:05:45.288 --> 00:05:46.747
there was a disclaimer
where somebody's like,

00:05:46.747 --> 00:05:48.350
"Hey, you're gonna have to
go out here and tell people

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:50.100
that Gary likes to say the F word a lot,

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:50.933
but then I was like,

00:05:50.933 --> 00:05:53.157
"Man, swearing is an intelligence thing,

00:05:53.157 --> 00:05:54.160
"marks intelligence."

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:56.580
So I was like, "You bet your butt we are."

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:57.413
Right?

00:05:57.413 --> 00:05:58.451
You know?

00:05:58.451 --> 00:05:59.284
- I appreciate it.
- That's like a dumb thing.

00:05:59.284 --> 00:06:00.350
(laughing)
- And listen,

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:02.020
Ryan told me back stage watch my mouth,

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:05.000
so I've thrown one shit out
and I've kept it fairly clean.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:05.833
I'm pretty pumped,

00:06:05.833 --> 00:06:07.960
but I know somebody's gonna
ask a fuckin' stupid question.

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:10.880
(laughing and clapping)

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:12.970
And I'm joking, 'cause
there is no stupid question.

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:14.580
On a very serious note,

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:16.480
and what I wanna set the tone on,

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:17.693
and this is where I wanna
inspire a couple of people

00:06:17.693 --> 00:06:18.940
that are still sitting

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:20.160
'cause they're either more introverted,

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:22.610
or lazy, or who the hell
knows why you didn't get up.

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:23.443
I

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:28.010
am really passionate about operations

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:30.110
and how to build an actual business.

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:33.730
And it's very hard to
produce content for that,

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:37.080
that can bring enough value and
that's why I don't go there.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:39.312
Listen, I think a lot of
you have a sense of me.

00:06:39.312 --> 00:06:42.610
There was a very long time
where I went nowhere close

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:45.480
to anything motivational
'cause I have zero

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:48.570
point zero interest in
being a motivational speaker

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:51.660
even though I know many,
many people view me that way.

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:53.590
I'm motivated.

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:55.190
I'm optimistic.

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:57.600
I'm deeply grateful and happy.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:00.320
And I genuinely do
believe that perspective

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:02.130
really, really matters.

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:04.860
Because if you think you've
lost before you've started,

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.970
you actually already lost and that's real.

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:09.070
'Cause that happens to me in things.

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:10.380
So

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:13.070
I have that in me, but I promise you,

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:15.720
please feel free to go very detailed.

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:17.767
I don't have a COO.

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:20.020
I have a thousand people.

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:23.080
I don't have a COO
'cause I'm operating it.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:26.000
I'm making tangible operational decisions

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.100
in the back room right now.

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:30.240
I've just been very, very thoughtful

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:33.760
of how to create content at
scale and post produced it,

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:36.600
contextual to the platforms that matter.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.500
But that doesn't take away
from the fact that I'm spending

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:41.900
11-14 hours a day being the CEO and COO

00:07:41.900 --> 00:07:43.560
of a thousand-person global agency.

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:45.110
So I have some thoughts.

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:46.540
Started from scratch,

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:47.519
so

00:07:47.519 --> 00:07:51.750
I can remember, and I understand,
and I know what has worked

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:53.540
for me and others that look like me

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:57.580
and what has kept a lot of
people at the $700,000 a year

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:58.850
in revenue business.

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:00.000
So I really think I can help.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.945
So please fire away.

00:08:01.945 --> 00:08:04.130
I'm honestly grateful to be
here and I appreciate it.

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:05.156
Thank you.

00:08:05.156 --> 00:08:08.085
(applauding)

00:08:08.085 --> 00:08:08.994
- [Robin] Hi, thank you, Gary.

00:08:08.994 --> 00:08:10.070
My name is...

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:10.970
Is this on?

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:14.210
My name is Robin Wilson and
I sat there all day long

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:17.000
because I knew that this 55-year-old woman

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.830
would only have a chance of getting here

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:21.460
if I was closest to the
mic and in the front row.

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:23.650
So strategy pays (laughing)
(cheering and applauding)

00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:24.900
- Hacking always works.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:26.210
- [Robin] Woo, love it.

00:08:26.210 --> 00:08:27.850
So I have

00:08:27.850 --> 00:08:28.910
a specific question.

00:08:28.910 --> 00:08:32.360
So I only do social media
marketing at our agency.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:34.960
We only do social and
email, but social mainly

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:36.480
on that forefront.

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:38.750
But we serve a very particular vertical.

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:40.470
We serve automotive.

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:41.840
So we're a woman-owned business,

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:43.700
do social media marketing.

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:46.520
Their leader's 55 years old,
like any of that gives a shit

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:47.460
about anything, right?

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:50.410
And we not only just serve
the automotive industry,

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:54.403
but we really kind of niche
with subprime dealerships.

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:57.020
That's kinda where our forte is,

00:08:57.020 --> 00:08:58.990
is that non-intender market.

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:00.890
And so my question has been

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:02.527
because people ask me all the time,

00:09:02.527 --> 00:09:04.210
"Do you guys do digital also?"

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:05.308
Which means search.

00:09:05.308 --> 00:09:08.760
And we don't because my
brain is only so big.

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:11.690
And so I don't know whether I
need to partner with somebody

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:12.523
or just continue

00:09:12.523 --> 00:09:15.250
to let them find their
outsourcing for that

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:17.670
because all digital isn't right.

00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:19.940
- I understand and do
you do paid and creative?

00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:21.280
Or just paid and just creative?

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:22.170
- [Robin] Paid and creative.

00:09:22.170 --> 00:09:23.003
- Understood.

00:09:23.003 --> 00:09:26.490
So I think the answer
is extremely personal.

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:28.720
I think you and everybody else here

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:31.479
is not unaware that when
you don't provide a service,

00:09:31.479 --> 00:09:33.450
it creates a vulnerability

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:35.760
that can lead to you
losing your service, right?

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:37.000
- [Robin] Right.
- Not super complicated.

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:38.050
We've all been there.

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:41.780
I think it comes down to,
and this is actually...

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:42.613
Thank you, Robin.

00:09:42.613 --> 00:09:44.340
This is a great way to start.

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:47.230
I'd literally backstage, just made a video

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:49.640
and for the people that
follow me the most,

00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:52.460
I'm in such post production,
film-my-life mode

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:54.780
that the days of five or six
years ago when I'd go straight

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:56.750
to camera with a thought video is rare.

00:09:56.750 --> 00:09:58.670
Original programming just for the video

00:09:58.670 --> 00:10:00.010
is rare for me these days,

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:01.610
but I'm so compelled right now

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:05.000
around this thought that
people are not self-aware

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:06.970
of what makes them happy
when they run a business.

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:08.660
And everybody just thinks about growth

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:10.770
without realizing the next employee

00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:12.770
or the next hundred
dollars is the beginning

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:16.050
of the process of you not
liking your business anymore.

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:17.210
And that's your answer.

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:19.130
Your answer is predicated on

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:21.270
you know it's a vulnerability.

00:10:21.270 --> 00:10:24.780
In one way, it's also a
strength in another way.

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:26.270
You just have to ask yourself

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:30.660
are you happy with the level
of business that you're at

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:33.910
and if you're not, are you in a place

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:37.590
where you think you can
get more deep narrow,

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:41.000
or do you think you
need to go wide, right?

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:42.750
Partnering is no.

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:43.750
Right?

00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:47.090
All partnerships are
vulnerable from the get.

00:10:47.090 --> 00:10:49.940
It's inconceivable that
another business or human

00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:52.090
has the same exact interest as you do

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:54.090
and something's gonna happen eventually.

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:57.070
Again, this is what makes this fun.

00:10:57.070 --> 00:10:58.800
The heads are nodding 'cause ya lived it.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:01.010
You already thought about the
shit you did that didn't work.

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:01.870
Right?

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:04.550
So that's why we never
partnered with anybody.

00:11:04.550 --> 00:11:06.400
As a matter of fact, I
never took a single meeting

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:07.390
