01:01:00.859 --> 01:01:01.692
Just business.

01:01:01.692 --> 01:01:03.590
People have a price for something.

01:01:03.590 --> 01:01:05.070
I'm always empathetic.

01:01:05.070 --> 01:01:06.620
They may have a P &amp; L issue.

01:01:06.620 --> 01:01:10.210
They may value me way
more than I'm even asking,

01:01:10.210 --> 01:01:13.540
but they can't for some other reason.

01:01:13.540 --> 01:01:16.200
But to your credit,

01:01:16.200 --> 01:01:18.810
you didn't think that,
that was an exchange.

01:01:18.810 --> 01:01:21.920
On the flip side, when
your company's very early,

01:01:21.920 --> 01:01:26.070
I think you eat crow at scale
because you need case studies.

01:01:26.070 --> 01:01:28.160
You need context, you know?

01:01:28.160 --> 01:01:29.220
- [Quentin] Makes sense.

01:01:29.220 --> 01:01:31.100
- It just didn't work for
you and that's okay to.

01:01:31.100 --> 01:01:32.152
There is no right answer.

01:01:32.152 --> 01:01:33.430
- [Quentin] Yes, sir.

01:01:33.430 --> 01:01:34.263
Appreciate it.

01:01:34.263 --> 01:01:35.096
Kimbo says, "What's up," by the way.

01:01:35.096 --> 01:01:36.051
- I love that.

01:01:36.051 --> 01:01:36.884
Thank you, Bro.

01:01:36.884 --> 01:01:39.380
(applauding)

01:01:39.380 --> 01:01:40.703
- [Man] Hi, Gary, what's going on, man?

01:01:40.703 --> 01:01:42.710
I just wanna say thank you.

01:01:42.710 --> 01:01:45.610
It's been just awesome hanging out here.

01:01:45.610 --> 01:01:47.740
- By the way, this is unbelievable.

01:01:47.740 --> 01:01:50.365
So I'm so sad right now and happy.

01:01:50.365 --> 01:01:54.620
Literally, I wanted to
extend this aggressively.

01:01:54.620 --> 01:01:56.767
On the queue here it says, "Last question.

01:01:56.767 --> 01:01:58.570
"Need to call your daughter."

01:01:58.570 --> 01:02:00.030
So I gotta go.

01:02:00.030 --> 01:02:01.020
But go quick.

01:02:01.020 --> 01:02:02.410
I'm so sorry for everybody.

01:02:02.410 --> 01:02:06.030
Just hit me up, but I clearly
use that to make you feel sad.

01:02:06.030 --> 01:02:07.847
(laughing)
- [Man] It works.

01:02:07.847 --> 01:02:12.847
So as a CEO, taking a
business working with clients

01:02:13.970 --> 01:02:15.970
that are bringing in $50
million to $100 mill,

01:02:15.970 --> 01:02:18.091
what was the mindset shift that you had

01:02:18.091 --> 01:02:20.270
to work with the big boys,

01:02:20.270 --> 01:02:22.150
the Fortune 500s?

01:02:22.150 --> 01:02:23.060
- Nothing.

01:02:23.060 --> 01:02:23.893
- [Man] Nothing.

01:02:23.893 --> 01:02:24.900
- Nothing.

01:02:24.900 --> 01:02:27.830
I let them come to me by
being historically correct

01:02:27.830 --> 01:02:30.683
with what their customer was going to do.

01:02:31.970 --> 01:02:33.740
The reason I win

01:02:33.740 --> 01:02:35.070
often

01:02:35.070 --> 01:02:37.920
is because I'm not worried
about eh person in the middle.

01:02:39.570 --> 01:02:40.620
Got it?
- [Man] Yeah.

01:02:40.620 --> 01:02:42.600
I didn't change for them.

01:02:42.600 --> 01:02:44.300
They changed for me.

01:02:44.300 --> 01:02:45.470
Why?

01:02:45.470 --> 01:02:46.933
Because I focused on you.

01:02:49.850 --> 01:02:53.010
The end customer is the leverage,

01:02:53.010 --> 01:02:55.910
not the relationship with the
person that writes the check

01:02:57.470 --> 01:02:58.943
if you're playing long.

01:03:02.270 --> 01:03:03.103
- [Man] Perfect.

01:03:03.103 --> 01:03:03.936
Thanks.

01:03:03.936 --> 01:03:04.774
Get to your daughter.

01:03:04.774 --> 01:03:06.390
(applauding)
- I love you guys.

01:03:06.390 --> 01:03:07.223
Thank you.

01:03:08.530 --> 01:03:09.523
Thank you so much.

01:03:10.790 --> 01:03:11.623
Thank you.

01:03:13.428 --> 01:03:15.901
[Man] Thanks, man appreciate it.

